<title>SOUTH AFRICA: S.AFRICAN AUG CONSUMER PRICE INDEX UP 7.5 PCT Y/Y.</title>
<headline>S.AFRICAN AUG CONSUMER PRICE INDEX UP 7.5 PCT Y/Y.</headline>
<dateline>PRETORIA 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Africa's all-items consumer price index rose 0.5 percent in August from July after rising 0.8 percent in July, the Central Statistical Service said.</p>
<p>The year-on-year rise was 7.5 percent versus July's 7.1 percent.</p>
<p>A Reuters consensus poll of economists forecast a 0.7 percent month-on-month increase and a 7.7 percent year-on-year rise.  </p>
<p>Pct changes:</p>
<p>			 Year/year			     Month/month</p>
<p>			 Aug '96    Jul '96  Aug '95  -  latest  prev</p>
<p>All items	     7.5	 7.1	7.5	   0.5     0.8</p>
<p>Lower income gp     7.5	 6.9	6.9	   0.7     0.9</p>
<p>Middle income gp    7.9	 7.5	7.5	   0.6     0.9</p>
<p>Higher income gp    7.3	 6.9	7.8	   0.5     0.7</p>
<p>Food only	     7.9	 4.8	2.0	   1.7     1.5</p>
<p>Indices:</p>
<p>			 Aug '96   Jul '96   Aug '95</p>
<p>All items	    184.8     183.8     171.9  </p>
<p>Lower income gp    183.0     181.8     170.2 </p>
<p>Middle income gp   188.0     186.9     174.2</p>
<p>Higher income gp   184.4     183.5     171.9</p>
<p>Food only	    210.3     206.8     194.9</p>
<p>(Index base 1990 = 100)</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom +27 11 482 1003</p>
